                <pb facs="0777" n="749" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v03/pg749"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">310.2/7–3054: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The United States Representative at the United
                        Nations</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Lodge</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Department of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1954-07-30T21:16:00-04:00">July 30, 1954—9:16
                            p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>102. Re Chinese representation: Deptel 46,
                    July 20 and our telegram 38, July 14. I attach greatest importance Department’s
                    plans make representations Embassies Washington and in appropriate capitals
                    (paragraph 3 Deptel 46). USUN has begun such representations in New York
                    and I hope Department’s efforts will proceed simultaneously.</p>
                <p>I understand Dixon (UK) will ask to see Secretary early next week and
                    suggest Secretary take up with him importance we attach to continuance
                    moratorium agreement. I was unable to reach Dixon as I indicated I would in my telegram 100, July 30.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lodge</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
